# Noma {id="nm-home"}

::summary{id="nm-home-summary"}
Noma is a plain-text document format (`.noma`) plus a hosted team workspace
(Noma Cloud) built on it. The format and Cloud are **one product**: pages are
readable source with stable block IDs, and agents edit them one block at a
time through proof, human approval, and a hash-checked apply. The current
release is **v0.19.0** (2026-09-26); five more Cloud work packages have
already merged to `main` under `[Unreleased]`.
::

This wiki is the curated entry point. It summarizes and links to the deep
docs in the repository (`docs/*.noma`, `PLAN.md`, `CHANGELOG.md`); it does
not replace them. When this wiki and the repo disagree, the repo wins —
file a Work issue labelled `dogfood` and fix the page.

## What Noma is {id="nm-home-what"}

One-liner from `docs/direction.noma`: *Noma is the wiki for the agentic-AI
era: a Confluence-class team wiki whose pages agents can safely edit.*

Since 2026-09-26 (`PLAN.md` §23.21) Noma is growing into one collaboration
surface for building software, with four parts over one permission model and
one source of truth:

::grid{columns=2}
:::card{title="Wiki (Confluence / Notion)"}
Spaces, page tree, labels, comments, history and diffs, restrictions,
macros, templates, attachments, a Visual block editor, and live co-editing.
Pages are `.noma` source and sync two-way with Git.
:::

:::card{title="Work (Jira)"}
Projects, issues, boards, and inline page tasks. Issues can be created from
a chat message in one step. Jira JSON imports into Work (unreleased).
:::

:::card{title="Chat (Slack)"}
Channels per project or topic, threads, DMs, files, ⌘K search. Agents are
members. A thread can be saved as a `.noma` page with one block per message.
:::

:::card{title="Run environments (ezkeel)"}
`/deploy` and `/test` in a project channel start a run on the ezkeel stack;
results post back to the thread and move the linked issue. Unreleased.
:::
::

The rule that ties them together: **chat must always be able to land in
source** — message → issue, thread → `.noma` page — so decisions end up in
reviewable, diffable text (`PLAN.md` §23.21).

