## Pages in this space {id="nm-home-map"}

| Page | Repo path | What it covers |
|---|---|---|
| Architecture | `wiki/noma/architecture.noma` | Format kernel, Cloud server, browser app, packages, PaperDOM fork, barrels |
| Roadmap | `wiki/noma/roadmap.noma` | Now / Next / Later, risks, decisions, agent follow-ups, dogfooding |
| Operations | `wiki/noma/operations.noma` | Dev setup, verification gates, releases, Cloud deploys, backups, env vars |
| Format cheat sheet | `wiki/noma/format.noma` | Block syntax, IDs and aliases, directives, patch ops, the proof loop |

The page tree follows the Git-native space layout: a page is `<slug>.noma`
and its children live in the `<slug>/` directory (`docs/noma-cloud.noma`,
"Git-native spaces").

